The (vanilla) game was considered inferior to Dks1 by a lot of players because:

-  the lack of world interconnectivity, and worse level design;

- the nonsensical geography and transitions from areas to areas;

- it lacks just memorable boss battles, and has too much bosses too, i also were considered repetitive (big guy with a goof);

- the game didn't know as good as the previews we saw, the person system they had was basically taken out from a game (probably to run on Ps3/Xbox360);

- gameplay would different from the similar games, and people had a hard time to adapt;

- things like adaptability (a stat that increases roll invincibility frames) and Soul Memory (the way matchmaking works) were perceived as bad and unnecessary changes.

Basically, vanilla version was a good game, but far from the senseless game that Dks1 was for a lot of people.

Now though, we got three dlcs, patches and this Scholar of the Punch Sin edition, which changes the game a lot.



The three Sides, is the best part of Dks2, and they do have the great level design Dks1 had. They also was cool gameplay mechanics, stuff, and a lot of armors, rings and quantities.

The Scholar edition is the best version available, it has all the shots, changes to the enemy placement, tons of new details it brings some life and secrets to areas.

